  "caveats": [
    "This is a *conjectural* bridge.  The Hückel rule is traditionally derived from molecular-orbital theory with the Hückel approximation; the topological derivation here uses only the T(2,N) component count and the parity of Δ_{T(2,N)}(1) = N/2.  Agreement is exact for N ∈ {2, 4, 6, 8, 10, 12, 14} but the bridge needs further work for the anti-aromatic case (cyclobutadiene, cyclooctatetraene), where Δ(1) = N/2 is *even* and the conjectural rule correctly predicts non-aromaticity but does not distinguish non-aromatic from anti-aromatic."
  ]
